<%- include('../../partials/header') %>
<%- include('../../partials/navigation', { user: (typeof user !== 'undefined' ? user : null) }) %>

<main class="bg-gray-50 py-24 min-h-screen">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 max-w-3xl">

        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6 tracking-tight">Review Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 mb-12">How we collect, check and publish customer feedback &mdash; and what we will not do.</p>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-[2rem] border border-gray-100 shadow-sm p-8 md:p-12 space-y-10 text-gray-700">

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-3">Our commitment</h2>
                <p class="leading-relaxed">
                    We publish only feedback that a real customer wrote. We do not display a rating,
                    an average or a review count that we cannot support with reviews that are
                    actually shown on this site. When we have no published reviews, we show no
                    rating at all.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-3">How to leave a review</h2>
                <p class="leading-relaxed mb-3">
                    Use the <a href="/reviews" class="text-brand-blue hover:underline font-bold">review form</a>.
                    We ask for your name or initials, an email address, a star rating, the service
                    you used and your comments. If you have an order number or company number,
                    providing it helps us verify you are a customer.
                </p>
                <p class="leading-relaxed">
                    <strong>Your email address is never published.</strong> We keep it only so we
                    can contact you about your review if we have a question.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-3">How reviews are published</h2>
                <ol class="space-y-3 list-decimal list-inside leading-relaxed">
                    <li>Every submission is read by a person before it appears on the site.</li>
                    <li>A review is labelled <strong>&ldquo;Verified customer&rdquo;</strong> only when we can match it to a completed order.</li>
                    <li>Unverified reviews may still be published, clearly marked as such.</li>
                    <li>Your wording is published as you wrote it. We do not rewrite reviews, and we do not ask for them to be softened.</li>
                </ol>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-3">What we do not remove</h2>
                <p class="leading-relaxed">
                    Negative reviews stay up. A one-star review from a real customer is more useful
                    to a prospective buyer than no review at all, and we would rather earn your
                    trust than protect a number.
                </p>
                <p class="leading-relaxed mt-3">
                    We remove a review only when it is spam, contains an attempt to inject links or
                    code, impersonates a customer, or discloses someone else's personal information.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-3">Incentives</h2>
                <p class="leading-relaxed">
                    We do not offer discounts, refunds or any other benefit in exchange for a
                    review, and we do not ask anyone to remove or change a review. If you were
                    offered something for reviewing us, please tell us and we will remove it.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-3">How ratings are calculated</h2>
                <p class="leading-relaxed mb-3">
                    The published rating is the arithmetic mean of every review shown on the site,
                    rounded to one decimal place. The review count is the number of reviews shown.
                    Both are calculated at page load from the reviews listed, so they cannot fall
                    out of step with what you can see.
                </p>
                <p class="leading-relaxed">
                    We do not weight reviews, remove low scores to move an average, or display a
                    different figure from the one the reviews produce.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-3">Illustrative examples</h2>
                <p class="leading-relaxed">
                    Some pages on this site contain illustrative founder scenarios that show the
                    kinds of problems we help solve. Those are examples, not customer testimonials,
                    and they are labelled as such where they appear. They are never counted towards
                    any rating.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-3">Corrections</h2>
                <p class="leading-relaxed">
                    If you believe a published review is misattributed to you, or you want your
                    details removed, contact us and we will action it. If we cannot verify that a
                    review came from you, we will remove it.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section class="border-t border-gray-100 pt-8">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-3">Contact</h2>
                <p class="leading-relaxed">
                    Email <a href="/contact" class="text-brand-blue hover:underline font-bold">our support team</a>
                    with the subject line &ldquo;Review correction&rdquo; and we will respond.
                </p>
            </section>

        </div>

    </div>
</main>

<%- include('../../partials/footer') %>
